thag10.5:4.1 starts: Linked together with a chain of bones,
thag10.5:4.2 starts: stitched together with tendon-threads,
thag10.5:4.3 starts: it produces its various postures,
thag10.5:4.4 starts: from being hitched up together.
thag10.5:9.1 starts: These who hold to this body as mine
thag10.5:9.2 starts: —blind fools, people run-of-the-mill—
thag10.5:9.3 starts: fill the horrific cemetery,
thag10.5:9.4 starts: taking on further becoming.
thag11.1:2.1 starts: As the monsoon wind
thag11.1:2.2 starts: drives the clouds in the rainy season,
thag11.1:2.3 starts: so thoughts concerned with seclusion
thag11.1:2.4 starts: impel me.
thag12.1:3.1 starts: The virtuous one, through restraint,
thag12.1:3.2 starts: acquires many friends,
thag12.1:3.3 starts: while the unvirtuous one, practicing evil,
thag12.1:3.4 starts: from friends is estranged.
thag10.1:10.1 starts: I am the son of the Buddha,
thag10.1:10.2 starts: Aṅgīrasa: incomparable, Such.
thag10.1:10.3 starts: You, Sakka, are my father’s father.
thag10.1:10.4 starts: In the Dhamma, Gotama,
thag10.2:1.1 starts: If, in front or behind,
thag10.2:1.2 starts: there is no one else,
thag10.2:1.3 starts: it’s extremely pleasant
thag10.2:1.4 starts: for one staying alone
thag10.2:6.1 starts: As I desire to do this,
thag10.2:6.2 starts: may my purpose succeed.
thag10.2:6.3 starts: I myself
thag10.2:6.4 starts: No one can do it
thag10.7:7.1 starts: Virtue, learning,
thag10.7:7.2 starts: investigating
thag10.7:7.3 starts: as they have come to be:
thag10.7:7.4 starts: This is fitting
thag11.1:7.1 starts: but never have I known
thag11.1:7.2 starts: “May these beings
thag11.1:7.3 starts: be slaughtered,
thag11.1:7.4 starts: fall into pain.”
thag11.1:9.1 starts: And the goal for which I went forth
thag11.1:9.2 starts: from home life into homelessness
thag11.1:9.3 starts: I’ve reached:
thag11.1:9.4 starts: the end
thag12.1:2.1 starts: Wise, one should protect one’s virtue,
thag12.1:2.2 starts: aspiring to three pleasures:
thag12.1:2.3 starts: praise, the gaining of wealth,
thag12.1:2.4 starts: and—after death—rejoicing in heaven.
thag12.1:5.1 starts: Virtue is the beginning, the establishing,
thag12.1:5.2 starts: the mother of what is fine,
thag12.1:5.3 starts: the foremost of all qualities:
thag12.1:5.4 starts: Therefore virtue should be purified.
